 "decisions": [
  {
   "title": "Single operation for the whole simulation",
   "context": "The screens call one action (Calcular) that validates, calculates and records the simulation. The rules are tightly linked: the rate feeds the installment, the installment feeds the total, and all of them feed the saved record.",
   "decision": "One use case, SimulateLoan, exposed as POST /simulations, implements RULE-001 to RULE-006. Calculation stays in pure domain code with no dependency on persistence. Only the save goes through the SimulationRepository port. Field names in the contract are camelCase identifiers (tasaAnual, cuotaMensual, totalPagar, numeroCorrelativo) and map to the snake_case screen fields and table columns.",
   "consequences": "The UI makes a single call and gets tasaAnual, cuotaMensual and totalPagar. Business errors are returned as a 422 response with the stable code and the exact message from the specification."
  },
  {
   "title": "Validation order and rejection without side effects",
   "context": "Both the amount and the term can be invalid at once, and the screen shows a single error message (mensaje_error). A rejected simulation must not be saved (RULE-006).",
   "decision": "The amount is validated first (AMOUNT_OUT_OF_RANGE), then the term (TERM_OUT_OF_RANGE). The range limits are inclusive: 1000.00 to 50000.00 and 6 to 60. Validation runs before any calculation or port call, so a rejection never touches the repository.",
   "consequences": "A rejected request leaves no record. If both values are invalid, only the amount message is returned."
  },
  {
   "title": "Rounding and numeric precision",
   "context": "The installment follows the French formula M x i / (1 - (1+i)^-n) with i = tasaAnual / 100 / 12. The specification requires 2 decimals with rounding half up. Examples: 10000.00 at 12.00 for 12 months gives 888.49; 5000.00 at 14.50 for 24 months gives 241.25.",
   "decision": "All money and rate arithmetic uses BigDecimal, never floating point. The intermediate steps (i, (1+i)^-n) use a high-precision MathContext (at least 20 digits). Only the final installment is rounded, to scale 2 with RoundingMode.HALF_UP. The total is the already rounded installment multiplied by the term, kept at scale 2 (888.49 x 12 = 10661.88). The rate comes from fixed bands: term <= 12 gives 12.00, 13 to 36 gives 14.50, 37 to 60 gives 16.00.",
   "consequences": "Results are deterministic and match the approved acceptance scenarios. The total can differ from monto plus interest by a few cents because it is based on the rounded installment, as the rule states."
  },
  {
   "title": "Persistence of accepted simulations for audit",
   "context": "RULE-006 requires each accepted simulation to be stored with a sequential number, amount, term, rate, installment, total and date/time.",
   "decision": "The accepted simulation is saved in table simulation. The numero_correlativo column is generated by the database (identity or sequence) and returned by SimulationRepository.save. fechaHora is taken from an injectable Clock in the domain, so it can be tested. The calculation and the save run in one transaction.",
   "consequences": "If the save fails, no result is returned and nothing is stored. Records are insert-only; no update or delete operations are defined."
  }
 ],
